## Generative Al enabled for instance

Enable/Disable Generative AI instance wide. Turning off generative AI in your instance will disable any feature that uses generative AI models. Features such as AI Chat, NLQ editor in Beast Modes and Views.

---

## Bring your own model to all product features

Enable all product features to use your models, defined in service settings, instead of Domo's default models. This will allow you to use your models for internal features like AI Chat, NLQ editor in Beast Modes and Views.

---

## DomoGPT

DomoGPT is a specialized AI engine powered by various state-of-the art models. All models powering DomoGPT are hosted in Domo's environment. Data used by these models never leaves our environment. This provider is essential for Domo AI to function properly.

---

## Domo Provided Models

The default models used in Domo allow for the following external providers. Disabling any of these external providers will change which models are used in your Domo instance. Disabling all providers will cause services to not work, if the Domo default is being used for the service.

---

## ML Connectors

Manage access to models provided by providers. Disabling providers will stop users in your instance from uploading models from that provider

